      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The author demonstrates that patients with ischemic heart disease have phenomenological peculiarities of adaptation by stability of thiol-dependent mechanism of structural-functional condition of blood serum proteins; describes the phenomenon of emergence of free nonprotein SH-groups in protein-free reaction mixtures of the serum varying in adrenaline concentrations in unstable angina pectoris (this phenomenon indicates structural-functional destabilisation of serum proteins and adequate immunopathological process); suggests an alternative method and pathogenetic diagnosis of IHD clinical forms in which thiol-containing analytes serve as molecular markers."},
